  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Monday)\nIssued at 1249 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nEarly this afternoon, we are still watching and waiting to see if\nwe can get some storms going. Thunderstorm chances are still\nhighly conditional and will depend on whether or not we can break\nthe cap. Yesterday, one storm was able to develop and as of this\nwriting, clouds are building over the central Black Hills. So it's\npossible.\n\nFor tonight, any storms that are able to develop, they will move\neast through the evening. Overnight looks quiet with diminishing\nwinds and overnight lows in the 50s to 60s.\n\nTuesday looks similar to today, with highs mostly in the upper \n80s to 90s. Zonal flow will keep the daily chances for afternoon \nstorms in place. SPC has placed a Slight (level 2 of 5) over the \ncentral SD counties for Tuesday.\n\nThe SPC has also placed a Slight risk of severe weather on \nWednesday over SW SD. Modest westerly winds aloft will be over the\ncentral High Plains Wednesday with a surface low developing near \nthe CO/KS border. Easterly surface winds north of the low over \nNebraska into southern South Dakota will maintain moisture and \ninstability into the area. Storms will form over the High Plains \nand move eastward through the evening. Hail may occur initially, \nwith damaging gusts possible during the evening.\n\nUnsettled pattern under zonal flow will give the area cooler \ntemps and daily chances for rain and storms for the second half of\nthe week.",
